    <selectionEntryGroup id="moc-special-skills" name="Marauder Special Skills" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true">
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry id="moc-skill-chosen" name="Chosen of Chaos" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade"><constraints><constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="moc-skill-chosen-max"/></constraints><rules><rule id="moc-skill-chosen-rule" name="Chosen of Chaos" hidden="false"><description>The Hero enters the rank of Chaos Warrior, uses the Warriors of Chaos maximum profile, and may use the Hero Equipment List.</description></rule></rules></selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="moc-skill-tattoo" name="Tattooed Body" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade"><constraints><constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="moc-skill-tattoo-max"/></constraints><rules><rule id="moc-skill-tattoo-rule" name="Tattooed Body" hidden="false"><description>Leader only. Eye of the Gods awards a Mark or creates a Spawn on 10+ instead of 12+ (11+ for a Norse leader).</description></rule></rules></selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="moc-skill-sweeping" name="Sweeping Blow" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade"><constraints><constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="moc-skill-sweeping-max"/></constraints><rules><rule id="moc-skill-sweeping-rule" name="Sweeping Blow" hidden="false"><description>Requires Strongman. When the Hero takes an enemy out of action with a double-handed weapon, immediately make another attack against a different model in base contact.</description></rule></rules></selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="moc-skill-mutant" name="Mutant" hidden="false" collective="true" import="true" type="upgrade"><rules><rule id="moc-skill-mutant-rule" name="Mutant" hidden="false"><description>The Hero may buy one mutation. A Hero with the Mark of Onogal may instead choose a Blessing of Nurgle other than Mark of Nurgle. This skill may be taken more than once.</description></rule></rules><entryLinks><entryLink id="moc-skill-mutations" name="Mutations" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" targetId="5541-f5c4-85e0-b399" type="selectionEntryGroup"/></entryLinks></selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="moc-skill-heart" name="Heart of the Warrior" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade"><constraints><constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="moc-skill-heart-max"/></constraints><rules><rule id="moc-skill-heart-rule" name="Heart of the Warrior" hidden="false"><description>Leader only. The Hero may re-roll failed Rout tests and is immune to fear and all alone tests.</description></rule></rules></selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>

    <selectionEntryGroup id="moc-marks" name="Marks of the Dark Gods" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true">
      <constraints><constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="moc-marks-max"/></constraints>
      <rules><rule id="moc-mark-limit" name="Marks of the Dark Gods" hidden="false"><description>Except for Chaos Undivided, the warband may never include models with different Marks. Seers choose a Mark when hired. A leader receives one only through Eye of the Gods.</description></rule></rules>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry id="moc-mark-undivided" name="Mark of Chaos Undivided" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade"><constraints><constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="moc-mark-undivided-max"/></constraints><rules><rule id="moc-mark-undivided-rule" name="Mark of Chaos Undivided" hidden="false"><description>Leader: warband members within the Leader radius may re-roll failed Leadership tests. Seer: the warband may include 0-3 Gors, which count toward its model maximum; re-roll The Lad&apos;s Got Talent results for them. A Seer uses Chaos Rituals.</description></rule></rules><entryLinks><entryLink id="moc-mark-chaos-rituals" name="Chaos Rituals" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" targetId="61c7-8179-00b5-1772" type="selectionEntryGroup"/></entryLinks></selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="moc-mark-tchar" name="Mark of Tchar the Eagle" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade"><constraints><constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="moc-mark-tchar-max"/></constraints><rules><rule id="moc-mark-tchar-rule" name="Mark of Tchar the Eagle" hidden="false"><description>Leader: becomes a spellcaster, learns one random Tchar Ritual, and suffers -1 on Difficulty rolls unless already a wizard. Seer: starts with two Tchar Rituals, one chosen and one random.</description></rule></rules></selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="moc-mark-arkhar" name="Mark of Arkhar the Dog" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade"><constraints><constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="moc-mark-arkhar-max"/></constraints><rules><rule id="moc-mark-arkhar-rule" name="Mark of Arkhar the Dog" hidden="false"><description>Leader: is subject to frenzy; spells targeting him fail on 4+. Seer: becomes a Bloodfather, cannot cast spells, and may take Strength skills. Each time he takes an enemy out in hand-to-hand combat, pass a Leadership test to add +1 to WS, S, T or I until battle end; each may increase once.</description></rule></rules></selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="moc-mark-onogal" name="Mark of Onogal the Crow" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade"><constraints><constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="moc-mark-onogal-max"/></constraints><rules><rule id="moc-mark-onogal-rule" name="Mark of Onogal the Crow" hidden="false"><description>Leader: +1 Toughness, immune to poison, and may re-roll once on the Serious Injuries table. Seer: uses Onogal Rituals and is immune to poison.</description></rule></rules></selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="moc-mark-shornaal" name="Mark of Shornaal the Serpent" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade"><constraints><constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="moc-mark-shornaal-max"/></constraints><rules><rule id="moc-mark-shornaal-rule" name="Mark of Shornaal the Serpent" hidden="false"><description>Leader: enemies not immune to psychology must pass a Leadership test on 3D6, discarding the lowest, before attacking him in close combat; on failure they are hit automatically, and once passed they need not retest that battle. Seer: uses Shornaal Rituals and, if not taken out, may brew unsellable Bugman&apos;s Ale instead of searching for a rare item.</description></rule></rules></selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
  </sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
  <catalogueLinks><catalogueLink type="catalogue" name="data" id="moc-data-link" targetId="e020-c282-277b-b173" importRootEntries="true"/></catalogueLinks>
